            <ArticleTitle>[Deterioration of lipid metabolism in testes under emotional-pain stress].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>40-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In severe emotional-pain stressor conditions alterations of lipid metabolism in rat testes appear to develop as a result of activation of peroxidation and lipolysis. These alterations may be important for stress impairment of the testes incretory function. Activation of pentose-phosphate pathway in stress-impaired testes is apparently one of mechanisms required for restoration of their structure and functions after the stress influence.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
